WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.196 --> 00:00:17.853
"That was a pretty awesome wipeout!"

2
00:00:17.854 --> 00:00:21.388
Riley looked up from where she was lying on the grass.

3
00:00:21.389 --> 00:00:28.206
Quinn Evans stood above her, holding out a bottle of water. "Thirsty?"

4
00:00:28.207 --> 00:00:37.367
"Thanks." Riley took the water and gulped down about half of it.

5
00:00:37.368 --> 00:00:45.288
"Yeah, I wiped out alright. I'm waiting for my mom to come. I think I need to get my ankle x-rayed."

6
00:00:45.289 --> 00:00:51.525
"Bummer," Quinn said. "My second run was three seconds faster than my first one.

7
00:00:51.526 --> 00:00:59.351
That's definitely good enough to make the team. I guess you're not going to be able to test the trail again today."

8
00:00:59.352 --> 00:01:07.865
Riley frowned. Maybe it was her imagination, but Quinn sounded almost pleased about Riley's fall.

9
00:01:07.866 --> 00:01:12.513
Just then Coach Adams hurried over.

10
00:01:12.514 --> 00:01:21.183
"Hey, Coach Adams!" Quinn burst out. "Did you see my time on that last run? I'm going to make a great Blue Demon!"

11
00:01:21.184 --> 00:01:27.247
The coach smiled at her. "If you repeat that time next weekend, you'll be doing well, Quinn."

12
00:01:27.248 --> 00:01:29.592
She tossed her head and smiled.

13
00:01:29.593 --> 00:01:34.095
"I need to talk to Riley for a minute, okay?" Coach Adams said.

14
00:01:34.096 --> 00:01:40.736
Quinn shrugged. "Sure, Coach," she said, walking away.

15
00:01:40.737 --> 00:01:47.647
Coach dropped onto the grass beside Riley. "How is the ankle?"

16
00:01:47.648 --> 00:01:52.875
"At least I'm not on a stretcher heading for the hospital," Riley said.

17
00:01:52.876 --> 00:01:58.556
She was trying to sound light and unconcerned, but instead her voice was tense.

18
00:01:58.557 --> 00:02:04.061
"It's not going to happen to you, you know," Coach Adams said quietly.

19
00:02:04.062 --> 00:02:12.459
"It wasn't supposed to happen to Jordan either," Riley said. "Nobody breaks a leg in four places, and gets a compound fracture.

20
00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:17.044
Jordan's injury was a one-in-a-million kind, according to the doctors."

21
00:02:17.045 --> 00:02:24.884
"Terrible things do happen sometimes. I've seen all kinds of injuries on the track." Coach Adams paused.

22
00:02:24.885 --> 00:02:34.608
"But you can't let fear, or Jordan's accident, affect your riding. Falling is part of the sport. Your fall today isn't a big deal."

23
00:02:34.609 --> 00:02:40.441
But the fall was a big deal to Riley. Blowing the jump wasn't the problem.

24
00:02:40.442 --> 00:02:44.700
Blowing her concentration and making stupid mistakes was.

25
00:02:44.701 --> 00:02:48.346
She couldn't let her mind drift away from the track.

26
00:02:48.347 --> 00:02:56.344
Ever since Jordan's accident, Riley had tried hard not to let jumps spook her. But sometimes it was impossible.

27
00:02:56.345 --> 00:03:01.002
And whenever she remembered Jordan's accident, it rattled her confidence.

28
00:03:01.003 --> 00:03:11.497
Just then Quinn rode past on her Fleet HD3. Riley and Coach Adams watched Quinn hit the track again.

29
00:03:11.498 --> 00:03:15.901
Her head was low, and she looked confident and skilled.

30
00:03:15.902 --> 00:03:21.652
"She's probably going to get one of the spots in the girls' junior division," Riley said.

31
00:03:21.653 --> 00:03:27.810
"You know what can be helpful when you need to focus?" Coach Adams said casually.

32
00:03:27.811 --> 00:03:33.141
Riley looked at him, ready to get any advice she could. "What?"

33
00:03:33.142 --> 00:03:43.627
He stood up. "Some good, old-fashioned competition. See you later, Riley. Good luck with the x-rays."

34
00:03:43.628 --> 00:03:52.311
Riley spent the afternoon at a walk-in clinic, having her ankle x-rayed.

35
00:03:52.312 --> 00:03:57.700
Just as Delaney had suspected, it wasn't broken, only sprained.

36
00:03:57.701 --> 00:04:05.794
"Will I be able to ride next Saturday?" Riley asked the doctor anxiously. "I'm supposed to try out for the Blue Demons team."

37
00:04:05.795 --> 00:04:10.469
"If you take it easy this week, I don't see why not," the doctor said.

38
00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:17.354
"Use ice packs to reduce the swelling, and be sure to keep your ankle elevated. You should be fine in a few days."

39
00:04:17.355 --> 00:04:24.187
"Did you hear that?" Mrs. Clark said, eyeing her daughter. "You've got to take it easy."

40
00:04:24.188 --> 00:04:28.287
"No worries, Mom. I'll be an angel."

41
00:04:28.288 --> 00:04:40.092
Riley's mom chuckled. "That'll be a first, sweetheart," she said, helping Riley hobble out of the exam room.

42
00:04:40.093 --> 00:04:49.594
For the next two days, Riley sat on the couch, icing her ankle and planning her winning strategy for next weekend's tryout.

43
00:04:49.595 --> 00:04:54.241
"Part one of my strategy is to get to the gym," she thought.

44
00:04:54.242 --> 00:04:58.651
She wanted to exercise her ankle and strengthen her leg muscles.

45
00:04:58.652 --> 00:05:03.339
Part two of her plan would be a lot more challenging.

46
00:05:03.340 --> 00:05:06.285
Her parents agreed to the gym idea.

47
00:05:06.286 --> 00:05:10.411
"That works well with our schedule too," Mr. Clark said.

48
00:05:10.412 --> 00:05:16.473
"You can meet Mom at the gym after school and do your thing. I'll take Jordan to physical therapy."

49
00:05:16.474 --> 00:05:25.393
On Tuesday afternoon after school, Riley's father picked her up and drove to the YMCA.

50
00:05:25.394 --> 00:05:29.876
Jordan was in the backseat with her crutches, playing games on her phone.

51
00:05:29.877 --> 00:05:35.533
"You'll meet Mom at the front desk," Dad instructed Riley as he parked out front.

52
00:05:35.534 --> 00:05:39.297
"Did you remember your membership card and all the forms?"

53
00:05:39.298 --> 00:05:43.728
Riley patted her backpack. "Right here."

54
00:05:43.729 --> 00:05:46.725
"And your ankle feels okay?"

55
00:05:46.726 --> 00:05:59.954
"It feels fine, Dad. I promise." Riley took a deep breath. Now it was time to put part two of the plan into action.

56
00:05:59.955 --> 00:06:04.023
"Dad," she blurted out before she could lose her nerve.

57
00:06:04.024 --> 00:06:09.020
"Did you know there are only two open spots for girls in the Blue Demons' junior division?"

58
00:06:09.021 --> 00:06:16.933
"No." He looked surprised. "I think you'll get one of them, sweetheart. You're a very skilled rider."

59
00:06:16.934 --> 00:06:22.851
"I'd be better, though," Riley went on, "if I had that new bike."

60
00:06:22.852 --> 00:06:26.774
Riley's parents had promised to help her buy a new bike this year.

61
00:06:26.775 --> 00:06:32.170
But after Jordan's accident, Riley's new bike was no longer a priority.

62
00:06:32.171 --> 00:06:38.830
On top of all the worry about Jordan's broken leg, medical bills kept coming and coming.

63
00:06:38.831 --> 00:06:44.003
"There's a really good new rider in my division," Riley said.

64
00:06:44.004 --> 00:06:52.654
She told her father about Quinn's expensive new bike. "I know we agreed that I would wait till summer for mine," she finished.

65
00:06:52.655 --> 00:06:58.560
"But maybe you guys could lend me the money now, before the tryout? Please?"

66
00:06:58.561 --> 00:07:08.966
Mr. Clark's smile had disappeared. "You definitely deserve a new bike," he said slowly. Riley's heart jumped.

67
00:07:08.967 --> 00:07:18.976
"But it's out of the question right now," he went on. "Once Jordan's medical bills are paid off, then maybe . . ."

68
00:07:18.977 --> 00:07:28.636
It was the answer she expected, but it still hurt. Riley slumped into the seat, fighting to keep back tears.

69
00:07:28.637 --> 00:07:35.621
"I know it's not fair," Mr. Clark said. "But it's the way it is right now."

70
00:07:35.622 --> 00:07:41.365
"I'm really sorry, Riley," Jordan said softly.

71
00:07:41.366 --> 00:07:49.286
Without a word Riley grabbed her backpack and jumped out of the car. Her mother was waiting in the lobby.

72
00:07:49.287 --> 00:07:57.348
"Hi, Riley. I . . ." Her words trailed off when she saw the stormy look on Riley's face. "What's the matter, honey?"

73
00:07:57.349 --> 00:08:00.255
"Nothing," Riley mumbled.

74
00:08:00.256 --> 00:08:04.587
Mrs. Clark looked hard at Riley but didn't ask any more questions.

75
00:08:04.588 --> 00:08:09.506
She just signed Riley in at the desk.

76
00:08:09.507 --> 00:08:17.346
"Be careful with that ankle," Mrs. Clark said. "I'm going to a yoga class. I'll meet you back here in an hour."

77
00:08:17.347 --> 00:08:28.487
"Fine," Riley muttered. And then she went off alone to work out.
